  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159650",
      "title": "Reserved File Names, Custom Components & How To Organize A NextJS Project",
      "lectureOrder": 91,
      "videoOrder": 85,
      "sourceHash": "787bdef91f0dcdd6b994c042cb5afd0dbe5bac054f2e4b4b39539b5e7b29fc49",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.81,
          "end": 2.73,
          "en": "Now there also are two other files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.73,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "in that app directory, which I haven't covered yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 8.43,
          "en": "And one is the globals.css file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.43,
          "end": 12.12,
          "en": "Now, in there I set up some CSS styles for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.12,
          "end": 16.2,
          "en": "and this file is being imported into the layout.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.2,
          "end": 19.26,
          "en": "so that it's essentially available on every page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 20.313,
          "en": "that's being loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 24.81,
          "en": "This is how you can import CSS files in NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.81,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "It's an approach that also works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "in most Vanilla React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 31.38,
          "en": "and this will then simply ensure that these styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 34.023,
          "en": "are made available on every loaded page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "Besides that, we also have an icon.png file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "and that's another special file name actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "If you add an image called icon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "it will be used as a favicon by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 51.96,
          "en": "Because you might've noticed that in the layout.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.96,
          "end": 56.04,
          "en": "we did not set up anything regarding a favicon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.04,
          "end": 59.61,
          "en": "so that little icon that shows up in the tab here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.61,
          "end": 62.37,
          "en": "for example, and yet we have one here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "if you take a close look,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 68.31,
          "en": "and that's the case because I added this icon.png file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.31,
          "end": 70.56,
          "en": "which uses this special icon name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.56,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "and if you add an image called icon directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "in the app folder as I am doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 78.033,
          "en": "this will be used as a favicon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.96000000000001,
          "end": 83.37,
          "en": "So as you can tell by now, the app folder is very important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.37,
          "end": 87.24,
          "en": "In there, you define your routes by adding folders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.24,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "and you have some reserved file names like page.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "icon.png, or layout.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 97.44,
          "en": "which then simply unlock different features, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.44,
          "end": 99.81,
          "en": "And for example, a route layout is needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.81,
          "end": 103.863,
          "en": "just as you need page.js files to really set up a route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 109.95,
          "en": "but you're not limited to these special files in NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.95,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "We can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 114,
          "en": "still also add regular React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114,
          "end": 117.03,
          "en": "which are not treated as pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 119.7,
          "en": "For that, let's say that we wanna put this image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.7,
          "end": 122.82,
          "en": "into this header into a separate component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.82,
          "end": 124.2,
          "en": "so that we cut it from here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.2,
          "end": 126.18299999999999,
          "en": "and we instead add it to a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.11,
          "end": 130.92,
          "en": "We could do that by adding a new JavaScript file anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 132.18,
          "en": "in that project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.18,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "for example, next to the page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 137.763,
          "en": "and we could name it header.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.02,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "By the way, you can also use .jsx as an extension also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 146.01,
          "en": "for those pages if you prefer that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.01,
          "end": 147.63,
          "en": "But here I'll stick to the default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.63,
          "end": 150.123,
          "en": "which was .js in this next project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.35,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "But now I added this file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 155.31,
          "en": "You could also name this Header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.31,
          "end": 157.62,
          "en": "with an uppercase starting character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.62,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "But here, since all these other default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "and important NextJS file names use lowercase names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "I'll stick to a lowercase name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 168.213,
          "en": "for my component file here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 172.62,
          "en": "But now in here we can export a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.62,
          "end": 174.483,
          "en": "a component function called header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.44,
          "end": 177.63,
          "en": "where we return a fragment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.63,
          "end": 180.933,
          "en": "and then in there, this image next to the h1 element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.31,
          "end": 186.15,
          "en": "So that's now again, a standard React component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.15,
          "end": 188.73,
          "en": "but now it's actually a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.73,
          "end": 190.86,
          "en": "that's not automatically picked up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.86,
          "end": 193.8,
          "en": "or handled by NextJS in any way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.8,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "It's not rendered as a layout or as a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 199.11,
          "en": "Instead, it's currently ignored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.11,
          "end": 202.233,
          "en": "because header is now not some special filename.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.61,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "We can of course import it now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.52,
          "end": 211.52,
          "en": "We can import it here into page.js like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.12,
          "end": 216.03,
          "en": "and then here we can output it just as you learned it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.03,
          "end": 218.07,
          "en": "with Vanilla React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.07,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "because we are still working with React here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 224.22,
          "en": "we are still working with components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 228.273,
          "en": "and JSX just enhanced with some extra features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 232.77,
          "en": "With that if you save that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.77,
          "end": 234.99,
          "en": "you see the same content as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.99,
          "end": 238.083,
          "en": "but now with that custom component being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.19,
          "end": 241.95,
          "en": "and you could really store this component anywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.95,
          "end": 244.92,
          "en": "we could also add a components folder here inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.92,
          "end": 248.073,
          "en": "of the app folder and move header.js in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 249.09,
          "end": 251.97,
          "en": "In that case, we just have to update the import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.97,
          "end": 254.04,
          "en": "and make sure that we import Header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.04,
          "end": 256.983,
          "en": "from ./components/header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 257.82,
          "end": 261.003,
          "en": "But with that being done, everything still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.35,
          "end": 266.13,
          "en": "Here, you also see the importance of page.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 269.7,
          "en": "because now that I added this components folder here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.7,
          "end": 272.73,
          "en": "you could think that we now should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.73,
          "end": 276.51,
          "en": "to visit /components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.51,
          "end": 278.94,
          "en": "but we would get a 404 error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.94,
          "end": 281.67,
          "en": "because this file in there is ignored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.67,
          "end": 284.34000000000003,
          "en": "by NextJS when it comes to routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.34000000000003,
          "end": 288,
          "en": "and we simply got no page.js file in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288,
          "end": 291.303,
          "en": "So that's how the Next App Router works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 292.65,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "Now, personally, I prefer to store my components outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 298.47,
          "en": "of that app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 298.47,
          "end": 300.99,
          "en": "but you can absolutely store them in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.99,
          "end": 304.32,
          "en": "And indeed, in the official NextJS documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 304.32,
          "end": 309.06,
          "en": "you can find an entire article that discusses different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.06,
          "end": 313.65,
          "en": "of structuring your NextJS projects and storing components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.65,
          "end": 316.47,
          "en": "Attached to this lecture, you find a link to this article",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 319.53,
          "en": "and you can simply pick the structure you personally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.53,
          "end": 320.523,
          "en": "like the most.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.6,
          "end": 325.2,
          "en": "I prefer to have my components outside of the app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.2,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "so that the app folder is just used for routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 330.453,
          "en": "and routing related tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.71,
          "end": 335.7,
          "en": "Now with that components folder moved out of header.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.7,
          "end": 339.69,
          "en": "you, of course, also again must update your import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 339.69,
          "end": 342.87,
          "en": "and here you can take advantage of another feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 342.87,
          "end": 346.74,
          "en": "that's typically unlocked in NextJS projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 346.74,
          "end": 351.51,
          "en": "where you can use an at symbol in your import paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.51,
          "end": 354.6,
          "en": "to refer to the root project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 354.6,
          "end": 357.423,
          "en": "So the root project outside of the app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 358.65,
          "end": 362.58,
          "en": "it's this jsconfig file that configures this alias,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.58,
          "end": 364.95,
          "en": "and that's simply a little convenience feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 364.95,
          "end": 368.31,
          "en": "which can simplify your import paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 368.31,
          "end": 371.34,
          "en": "because now I can simply refer to the root project folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 371.34,
          "end": 374.79,
          "en": "with at, and then they dive into the components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 374.79,
          "end": 376.953,
          "en": "and target the header.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 377.91,
          "end": 380.79,
          "en": "That's how we can use this feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.79,
          "end": 383.94,
          "en": "And with all that, again, we got the same content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 383.94,
          "end": 386.73,
          "en": "as before if we visit the starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.73,
          "end": 389.703,
          "en": "but now with that outsourced components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
